# CloudWatch Log Monitoring on EC2

## 1. Create IAM Role

Go to:

**AWS Console → IAM → Roles → Create Role**

Select:

```text
Trusted entity: AWS service
Use case: EC2
```

For permissions, attach:

```text
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
```

Create the role and attach it to your EC2 instance.

> The IAM role allows the CloudWatch Agent to send logs and metrics to AWS CloudWatch without storing AWS Access Keys on the EC2 instance.

---

## 2. Update Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt update -y
```

---

## 3. Download CloudWatch Agent

For Ubuntu 64-bit:

```bash
wget https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/ubuntu/amd64/latest/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
```

---

## 4. Install CloudWatch Agent

```bash
sudo dpkg -i -E ./amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
```

---

## 5. Configure CloudWatch Agent

Run:

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-config-wizard
```

During the wizard, select the log file that you want to monitor.

For example:

```text
/var/log/syslog
```

You will also be asked for:

```text
Log Group Name
Log Stream Name
Initial Position
```

Example:

```text
Log Group Name: /ec2/syslog
Log Stream Name: {instance_id}
Initial Position: From start of file
```

The wizard will create a configuration file.

---

## 6. Start the CloudWatch Agent

If the configuration file is located at:

```text
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/config.json
```

Run:

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl \
-a fetch-config \
-m ec2 \
-s \
-c file:/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/config.json
```

---

## 7. Check CloudWatch Agent Status

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl \
-a status \
-m ec2
```

The agent should show:

```text
running
```

---

## 8. Check Logs in CloudWatch

Go to:

**AWS Console → CloudWatch → Logs → Log groups**

Open the log group that you configured.

You should see the logs from your EC2 instance.

---

## Important

Do NOT use:

```bash
curl https://s3.amazonaws.com/aws-cloudwatch/downloads/latest/awslogs-agent-setup.py -O
```

and do NOT use:

```bash
sudo python3 ./awslogs-agent-setup.py
```

These commands belong to the old CloudWatch Logs Agent setup.

Also, do not enter or upload AWS Access Keys and Secret Keys on the EC2 instance. Use the IAM role attached to the EC2 instance.
